    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d619">

                <pb facs="0947" n="926" xml:id="pg926"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.111/10–648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in the
                        Soviet Union </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-06T18:00:00-05:00">October 6, 1948—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1202. Reference restrictions as originally applied Emb stated “Authorities have
                    made it abundantly clear that travel in the Soviet Union to the virtually
                    all-inclusive enumerated areas is absolutely forbidden without prior official
                    authorization” (Embtel 1025 May 22, 1941<anchor n="1" xml:id="d619-f1"/>)
                    Accordingly retaliatory restrictions provided Dept’s note Jun 7, 1941 to Sov Amb
                    required prior permission riot merely notification for travel outside Washington
                    and vicinity. Important have full clarification present practice (reurtel 2245
                    Oct 4<anchor n="2" xml:id="d619-f2"/>) in considering possible retaliation now.
                    Proposed trip MA Stalingrad will not clarify this point since he had requested
                    permission travel nor do queries contemplated note appear cover it.</p>
                <p>Leningrad, Stalingrad, Odessa included in enumerated areas 1941 (Emb’s 991, May
                    17, 1941<anchor n="3" xml:id="d619-f3"/>). Gilmore<anchor n="4" xml:id="d619-f4"
                    /> despatch today states Leningrad, Odessa not on restricted list but does not
                    mention Stalingrad. Clarify.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
